# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository. Turtle and TSV are also LF in the
# working tree: the specification gates and the engine compare them byte-for-byte after
# parsing multi-line literals, and a CRLF checkout puts carriage returns inside them.
* text=auto
*.ttl text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
# The conformance suite's case files are compared byte for byte with what tools/conformance/
# generates, and its inputs are binary: no line-ending conversion, in the index or the working tree.
specification/conformance/physical-parser/** -text
specification/conformance/semantic-emitter/** -text
specification/conformance/bundle-processor/** -text
specification/conformance/hdl-compiler/** -text
specification/conformance/conformance-evaluator/** -text
